<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tupua Tamasese Titimaea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1891</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tupua Tamasese Titimaea was a Samoan paramount chief who was installed as king with German backing in 1887, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> deposed and exiled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malietoa-laupepa">Malietoa Laupepa</a>. His rule provoked a rising led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mataafa-iosefo">Mataʻafa Iosefo</a>, and the resulting crisis brought German, American and British warships to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apia">Apia</a> in 1889. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-berlin-1889">Treaty of Berlin</a> of that year restored Laupepa, and Tamasese died in 1891.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tupua-tamasese-titimaea.jpg" alt="Tupua Tamasese Titimaea" width="254" height="379" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: not mentioned · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tupua_Tamasese_Titimaea.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
